# MERN Lab Task 1 — CRUD + Sign Up

This project contains two independent lab exercises based on the supplied screenshots.

## Part A: CRUD operations on an array (HTML, CSS, Express.js, REST API)

Requirements: Node.js 18+.

1. Open a terminal in `part-a-crud`.
2. Install dependencies: `npm install`
3. Start the server: `npm start`
4. Open http://localhost:3000

The server stores items in a JavaScript array, so changes reset when the server restarts. This is intentional for the array-based task.

REST endpoints:
- `GET /api/items` — list items
- `GET /api/items/:id` — fetch one item
- `POST /api/items` — create item (`{"name":"Book","price":250}`)
- `PUT /api/items/:id` — update item
- `DELETE /api/items/:id` — delete item

## Part B: React sign-up + Express REST API + MongoDB

Requirements: Node.js 18+ and a MongoDB instance (local or MongoDB Atlas).

1. Start MongoDB and ensure its connection URI is available.
2. Open a terminal in `part-b-signup/server`.
3. Run `npm install`.
4. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`, then set `MONGO_URI` and `JWT_SECRET`.
5. Run `npm start` (API runs on http://localhost:5000).
6. In another terminal, open `part-b-signup/client`.
7. Run `npm install`, then `npm run dev`.
8. Open the Vite URL shown in the terminal (usually http://localhost:5173).

Sign-up endpoint: `POST /api/auth/signup` with `{ "email": "...", "password": "..." }`.
Login endpoint: `POST /api/auth/login` with the same fields.
Passwords are hashed using bcrypt before storage. The API returns a JWT after successful sign-up/login. Do not use the example JWT secret in production.
